To achieve dark mode with a black background and white text across components, I would recommend using a CSS variable for the text color to allow for easy swapping between light and dark modes.

```css
:root {
  --text-color: white;
}

body {
  background-color: black;
  color: var(--text-color);
}
```

Then, simply change the `--text-color` variable to swap between light and dark text color schemes.

```css
body.light {
  --text-color: white;
}

body.dark {
  --text-color: white;
}
```

This will change all text to white across the page with the dark mode switch.

For specific component colors, use the same variable:

```css
.component {
  background-color: var(--primary-color);
  color: var(--text-color);
}

body.light.component {
  background-color: var(--light-primary-color);
}

body.dark.component {
  background-color: var(--dark-primary-color);
}
```

This abstracts color changes and keeps them consistent across the app.

To toggle dark/light mode, use a flag in your state management system or a toggle button that changes the body class to `.light` or `.dark`. For example with a button:

```javascript
const [darkMode, setDarkMode] = useState(false);

const toggleDarkMode = () => setDarkMode(!darkMode);
```

